WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:05.749
CISA's Zero Trust Maturity Model defines
an identity as attributes that describe,

2
00:00:05.749 --> 00:00:09.925
quote, an agency user or entity,
including non-person entities.

3
00:00:09.925 --> 00:00:13.900
So service accounts are inside the
Identity pillar, not beside it.

4
00:00:13.900 --> 00:00:18.477
The guide scores three kinds of service
identity against the pillar's functions:

5
00:00:18.477 --> 00:00:22.712
authentication, identity stores, risk
assessments and access management.

6
00:00:22.712 --> 00:00:24.097
The stages are CISA's;

7
00:00:24.097 --> 00:00:28.100
where each kind lands is the
program's reading, design guidance.

8
00:00:28.100 --> 00:00:29.338
Authentication.

9
00:00:29.338 --> 00:00:33.790
CISA's Traditional stage is passwords
or multi-factor authentication;

10
00:00:33.790 --> 00:00:36.462
Optimal continuously validates identity.

11
00:00:36.462 --> 00:00:40.923
A user account used as a service
is Traditional: a static password,

12
00:00:40.923 --> 00:00:45.137
often never expiring, and crackable
offline if it holds an S P N.

13
00:00:45.137 --> 00:00:49.458
A G M S A or a D M S A is better
than Traditional on the credential,

14
00:00:49.458 --> 00:00:53.259
because it's generated,
rotated and unknown to people,

15
00:00:53.259 --> 00:00:57.925
but its Kerberos access is static,
with no continuous evaluation.

16
00:00:57.925 --> 00:01:02.011
An Entra workload identity is
token-based, short-lived and logged,

17
00:01:02.011 --> 00:01:05.113
and a managed identity has
no credential to steal.

18
00:01:05.113 --> 00:01:09.449
Microsoft Learn says workloads can't
perform multifactor authentication,

19
00:01:09.449 --> 00:01:12.340
so the workload equivalent
of phishing-resistant

20
00:01:12.340 --> 00:01:15.575
multifactor authentication
is having no stored secret.

21
00:01:15.575 --> 00:01:16.950
Identity stores.

22
00:01:16.950 --> 00:01:19.831
Traditional is self-managed,
on-premises stores;

23
00:01:19.831 --> 00:01:24.225
Optimal securely integrates them
across all partners and environments.

24
00:01:24.225 --> 00:01:29.725
The user account and the G M S A both live
only in on-premises Active Directory.

25
00:01:29.725 --> 00:01:32.282
The workload identity lives in Entra I D,

26
00:01:32.282 --> 00:01:36.720
the program's integrated store, and
federation reaches other clouds.
